  "notes": "Master-G MGA3200 (manufacturer SCBC, device R1, Realtek platform), Android TV 9 (API 28), 1.5 GB\nRAM, 1280x720 output. Firmware PTT1.201001.001 build 259 (2020-12-23), security patch 2020-11-05.\nThe OS itself reports model/device strings \"ATV R1\"/\"R1\" on this TV — same hardware:\nfingerprint MASTER-G/MASTER-G/R1:9/PTT1.201001.001/259:user/release-keys\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/master-g-mga3200/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/master-g-mga3200/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nSame SCBC platform and Realtek board family as examples/thomson-t32rtl6000/ and examples/sanyo-atv-r2/\n(SCBC, PTT1.x firmware branch).\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (restore.sh / build-and-install.sh defaults work).\nLive TV app: com.android.tv with the Realtek ISDB-T tuner stack (com.realtek.dtv, com.realtek.tv.isdb) —\nthe tuner must stay enabled or digital broadcast channels disappear.\nKept on purpose: GMS / Play / WebView / keyboard, remote/Bluetooth (com.apps.smartkey,\nbluetoothremote, fivekey, virtualkey, autopair, com.realtek.keyinterceptserver),\ncom.creative.fastscreen.tv (FastCast Miracast receiver — NOT ad bloat), and streaming apps left to taste.\n--- Telemetry, analytics, recommendation rows ---",
